<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=tank">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Weapons and war</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tank</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1915">1915</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as landship</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A tank is an armoured fighting vehicle combining heavy firepower, strong armour and the mobility of tracks and a powerful engine; the first British prototype, Little Willie, was built at William Foster &amp; Co. in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lincoln-england">Lincoln, England</a>, in 1915. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> developed tanks separately and at the same time to break the deadlock of trench warfare in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>; no single inventor can be named, though Walter Gordon Wilson and William Tritton played leading roles. The British Mark I first went into battle at the Somme in September 1916.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tank.jpg" alt="Tank" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain News Service · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mark_I_series_tank.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1915</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Lincoln, England</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Walter Gordon Wilson · William Tritton</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>France (1915)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>No single inventor can be named, and earlier designs, from Leonardo da Vinci’s to Lancelot de Mole’s of 1911, were never built.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/internal-combustion-engine">Internal combustion engine<span>1794</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/maxim-gun">Machine gun<span>1884</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=tank">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
